  "name": "Tinker War Crimes only procs from the sources it names (#3115)",
  "contract": "#3115: War Crimes (707239) reads 'Damage dealt by Explosive Augmentation and Tracer Augmentation now has a 50% chance to apply an additional stack of Napalm to enemies'. Spell.dbc row 707239 carries ProcFlags 0x15510 - every direct Tinker spell hit of any source - an empty effect class mask and ProcChance 50, and nothing in the repository bound it, so the generated proc entry applied Napalm (805315) from any Tinker spell instead. Fail-before proof: Overload (705798), a Tinker damage spell that is neither named source, must never apply Napalm. It is SPELL_DAMAGE_CLASS_MELEE, so each landed hit raises PROC_FLAG_DONE_SPELL_MELEE_DMG_CLASS, one of the flags in 0x15510, and is an independent 50% roll on the current code; 20 hits inside Napalm's 8000 ms duration (SpellDuration row 31) leave a 1 in 2^20 chance of a clean target. After the fix the script restricts the proc to 653238 and 653247 and this assertion is deterministic. The other half of the report - that the two named sources now reach the proc - is not asserted here: both deliver their damage at the 1500 ms global cooldown at best, Napalm lives only 8000 ms, and the harness has no any-of-N assertion, so a 50% roll cannot be observed without a false-failure rate of several percent.",
